Subject: [PATCH 1/2] jails: Persist lab-claude's claude dir
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: yvwzvomxwvurnqystrzsozvmrprtrqqs

~claude/.claude sits on the jail root dataset, so just clean destroys
it along with Claude's credentials, settings, history, and project
state. Every rebuild then means logging in and setting up again.

Mount it from /jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude, outside the dataset
clean destroys, so it survives a rebuild. The jail starts before its
users exist; pw useradd -m takes the home directory exec.prepare made
and chowns it to the user.
---
change-id: yvwzvomxwvurnqystrzsozvmrprtrqqs

 jails/README.org                     | 5 +++++
 jails/instances/lab-claude/jail.conf | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/jails/README.org b/jails/README.org
index 77d764b..bc5c1e8 100644
--- a/jails/README.org
+++ b/jails/README.org
@@ -5,8 +5,13 @@
 #+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
 /jails/share/lab.git
 /jails/share/lab-submissions.git
+/jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude
 #+END_EXAMPLE
 
+=/jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude= holds lab-claude's =~claude/.claude=,
+so it persists across =just clean=.  Own it by uid and gid 15000, the
+jail's =claude= user.
+
 Install the shared jail defaults once, before building or running any
 jail. Each instance jail.conf includes it by absolute path:
 #+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-claude/jail.conf b/jails/instances/lab-claude/jail.conf
index 564d94d..bfeacd6 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-claude/jail.conf
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-claude/jail.conf
@@ -10,6 +10,10 @@ lab-claude {
   exec.prepare += "mkdir -p ${path}/data/lab-submissions.git";
   mount += "/jails/share/lab-submissions.git ${path}/data/lab-submissions.git nullfs rw 0 0";
 
+  # ~claude/.claude lives outside the jail root so it survives a rebuild.
+  exec.prepare += "mkdir -p ${path}/home/claude/.claude";
+  mount += "/jails/data/lab-claude/dot-claude ${path}/home/claude/.claude nullfs rw 0 0";
+
   allow.mount;
   allow.mount.devfs;
   allow.mount.fdescfs;
